  <h1>Why Should Students Choose BCA in 2026?</h1>

  <p>
    Technology is transforming every industry. From banking and
    healthcare to education and e-commerce, businesses are
    becoming more digital. If you have completed Class 12 and
    want to build a career in Information Technology, Bachelor
    of Computer Applications (BCA) can be an excellent option.
  </p>

  <h2>What Is a BCA Degree?</h2>
  <p>
    Bachelor of Computer Applications (BCA) is an undergraduate
    degree focused on computer applications, programming,
    databases and information technology. The duration and
    curriculum depend on the university.
  </p>

  <h2>Why Choose BCA in 2026?</h2>
  <h3>1. Growing IT Career Opportunities</h3>
  <p>
    BCA students can develop skills in software development,
    networking, databases, IT support and system administration.
  </p>

  <h3>2. Learn Cloud Computing</h3>
  <p>
    Cloud platforms such as AWS, Microsoft Azure and Google
    Cloud are important parts of modern IT infrastructure.
    Learning cloud fundamentals can help students prepare
    for relevant entry-level roles.
  </p>

  <h3>3. Explore Cyber Security</h3>
  <p>
    Cyber Security focuses on protecting computer systems,
    networks and information. Students can learn networking,
    security fundamentals and authorized lab practices.
  </p>

  <h3>4. Develop Practical Skills</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Python Programming</li>
    <li>Linux Administration</li>
    <li>Computer Networking</li>
    <li>SQL and Database Management</li>
    <li>Cloud Computing Fundamentals</li>
    <li>Cyber Security Fundamentals</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Career Opportunities After BCA</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Software Developer</li>
    <li>Web Developer</li>
    <li>Technical Support Engineer</li>
    <li>Network Engineer</li>
    <li>Cloud Support Associate</li>
    <li>Cyber Security Analyst</li>
    <li>System Administrator</li>
  </ul>

